From 8c9a9f3c88bacab61cd873f52c07092badf1abcc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mauricio Chirino <1657723+mchirino89@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 15:52:04 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(ios): add setFoldPosture for foldable simulators

Adds a `setFoldPosture` command that folds a foldable iOS simulator
(iPhone Duo, Xcode 27.1+) to `closed`, `halfFold` or `flat`.

simctl exposes no hinge control, so the driver compiles a small helper
from `hinge_helper.c`, spawns it inside the simulator, and posts the
private vendor-defined HID event that Device Hub's hinge slider sends.
The resulting angle is read back through `devicectl device motion
hinge-angle`, which catches both a simulator that cannot fold and a
future Xcode that changes the private event -- `optional: true`
downgrades either failure to a warning.

The YAML shape follows `pressKey`: a `@YamlValues` String plus a
delegating creator, so the published schema describes the command
without a hand-written deserializer. Drivers that cannot fold inherit a
default that fails with a clear message.

Tent, vertical and split-screen postures are left out: the hinge only
spans 0-180 degrees, so an angle alone cannot separate laptop from tent,
and nothing in simctl or devicectl drives split-screen.

Refs #3617

