From faf64e5fe4d2cb8927fed20046404f7e9007b179 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mauricio Chirino <1657723+mchirino89@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 18:21:57 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] fix(ios): fail setFoldPosture as a command, not a crash

Running setFoldPosture against a non-foldable simulator killed the whole
run with an unhandled SimctlError: Orchestra only downgrades
MaestroException, so `optional: true` could not warn and the flow never
reached its next command.

Map anything that is not an IOSDeviceErrors to
MaestroException.InvalidCommand, keeping the underlying message.

Verified on a booted iPhone 17 Pro: the command now reports FAILED with
"... did not report a hinge angle ...", and WARNED with `optional: true`
while the rest of the flow runs. The iPhone Duo path is unchanged.

Refs #3617

