From b3f2d9cf8f453a10525f1e714878a20a8d451f09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mauricio Chirino <1657723+mchirino89@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 10:34:07 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] fix(ios): read the fold back from the displays when
 hinge-angle is gone

Xcode 27.1 RC removed `devicectl device motion hinge-angle` (it now
exits 64, "Unknown option '--device'"), so every `setFoldPosture` on a
Duo failed with "did not report a hinge angle" even though the hinge
moved.

When that command yields no angle, read `devicectl device info displays
--json-output -` instead: an open Duo lights its inner display (not the
primary one), a closed one only the outer. That tells closed from open,
not halfFold from flat; a simulator with one display still fails with
the same message as before. Older Xcodes that still stream the angle
keep the exact check.

Verified on the 27.1 RC: closed, flat, halfFold, flat, closed all
COMPLETED on an iPhone Duo; an iPhone 17 Pro (iOS 26.5) still fails the
command (WARNED with `optional: true`).

